    "q-72477": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72477",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,2]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}2Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}2Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that both ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are equal to the length of the interval $[1,2].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-1=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining our results, we have \n\n$$\n2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1=2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
