    "q-123067": {
      "dom_id": "step-q123067",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[1,3]$ and $[3,6]$ respectively. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-1=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-3=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
