    "q-123075": {
      "dom_id": "step-q123075",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-3,-1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-2,1]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-2,1].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=1-(-2) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-2)\\cdot (-8)\\cdot 3=48.\n$$",
